  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young African Leaders Initiative (YALI) - Niger Bio-Plast</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigerbioplast is a company dedicated to environmental protection through the sale of their mobile toilets, of which 80% are made from recycled materials such as pallets. To avoid water contamination from public defecation, septic tanks will be built with a system of bacterial drain to protect populations from fecal-oral diseases. Two toilets will be installed in each Senegalese commune. The use of these toilets will be charged against a sum of 0.16 dollars per passage. For each toilet a woman will be hired to take care of the maintenance and collection of user fees. This will raise the coverage rate to 100% for the municipalities and will reach 10% of the city&apos;s population.</narrative>
  </description>
